-- title:
--   Finiteness over a precomplete local ring from the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative local ring which is precomplete for its maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, in the sense that every sequence in $\mathcal{O}$ that is Cauchy for the $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$-adic filtration admits a limit, and let $A$ be a commutative local ring equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure such that $A$ is Hausdorff for its own maximal ideal, i.e. $\bigcap_n \mathfrak{m}_A^n A = 0$, and such that the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to A$ is a local homomorphism (the preimage of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ is $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, in the form: non-units are sent to non-units). Assume that the special fibre $A/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}A$, the quotient of $A$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ under the structure map, is a finitely generated $\mathcal{O}$-module. Then $A$ itself is a finitely generated $\mathcal{O}$-module. No noetherian or separatedness assumption is placed on $\mathcal{O}$, and $A$ is not assumed complete, only Hausdorff.
--
--   This is the topological Nakayama lemma in the form appropriate to a local algebra over a precomplete local base: finiteness of a module descends from the special fibre. It supplies the finiteness step for the freeness statement [`MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.exists_coords_of_quotient_span_finite_free), where the base is a power series ring over $\mathcal{O}$ and the quotient by an explicit ideal is finite and free.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Finite_of_finite_quotient_map_maximalIdeal.lean

